{"annotator_prompt": [
 {"kind": "modify", "field": "pending_cubes", "edits": [
  {"modify_from": "Ordered list of [y, x] positions of cubes that sit on highlighted white areas and have not yet been picked up.", "modify_to": "Unordered set, written as a list, of the [y, x] positions of cubes that sit on highlighted white areas and have not yet been picked up; the order of entries carries no meaning and is never used to choose a cube."},
  {"modify_from": "sorted by x from largest to smallest (the robot's leftmost cube first), regardless of the order in which the highlighted areas are listed.", "modify_to": "in the order the highlighted areas are listed in the observation."}
 ]},
 {"kind": "modify", "field": "button_pressed", "edits": [
  {"modify_from": "`yes` at every step from the one whose execution steps show the button pressed down (gripper descended onto the button) onward, i.e. from step #2 to the end of the episode.", "modify_to": "`yes` at every step from the one whose execution steps show the press onward, i.e. from step #2 to the end of the episode. The press is shown by EITHER of two signs: the button labelled pressed down, OR the gripper at the button's [y, x] (within a few pixels) at a height near 0.03 with fingers closed (0-2% open); the highlighted areas vanishing afterwards confirms it. Either sign alone is the press. Never reverts to `no`."}
 ]}
],
"policy_prompt_for_memory": [
 {"kind": "modify", "field": "button_pressed", "edits": [
  {"modify_from": "Write `no` when the memory carried in says `no` (or is empty) and no execution step in front of you shows the button pressed down.", "modify_to": "Write `no` when the memory carried in says `no` (or is empty) and no execution step in front of you shows the press (neither the pressed-down label nor the gripper at the button's position at low height with closed fingers)."},
  {"modify_from": "Write `yes` as soon as any execution step shown at this step says the button is pressed down, or the memory carried in already says `yes`.", "modify_to": "Write `yes` as soon as any execution step shown at this step either says the button is pressed down, or shows the gripper within a few pixels of the button's [y, x] at a height of about 0.02-0.04 with fingers nearly closed (0-2% open); the highlighted areas then vanish from the listing before the decision step, which confirms the press. Either sign alone is enough; do not wait for the label. Write `yes` also whenever the memory carried in already says `yes`."}
 ]},
 {"kind": "modify", "field": "pending_cubes", "edits": [
  {"modify_from": "Ordered list of [y, x] of cubes on highlighted white areas not yet picked up.", "modify_to": "Unordered set, written as a list, of the [y, x] of cubes on highlighted white areas not yet picked up; the order of entries carries no meaning and is never used to choose a cube."},
  {"modify_from": "and sort the entries by x from largest to smallest (the robot's leftmost cube first), not in the order the areas are listed.", "modify_to": "in the order the areas are listed."}
 ]}
],
"policy_prompt_for_subgoal": [
 {"modify_from": "1. If button_pressed is `no` (or memory is empty) and no execution step in front of you shows the button pressed down: choose A, press button.", "modify_to": "1. Choose A, press button, only when the button_pressed value you write at THIS step is `no`: that is, the memory carried in says `no` or is empty AND no execution step shown here shows the press (neither the pressed-down label nor the gripper at the button's position at low height with closed fingers). Every rule below likewise uses the button_pressed and pending_cubes values written at this step, not the carried ones."},
 {"modify_from": "choose B, pick up the highlighted cube, pointing at the FIRST entry of pending_cubes (the list is sorted with the robot's leftmost cube, largest x, first). Point at that stored [y, x], or at the cube visible within a few pixels of it (cube positions wobble). If no cube is currently listed at that position it is merely hidden by the arm: still choose B at the stored point; never skip to a later entry and never treat the list as empty.", "modify_to": "choose B, pick up the highlighted cube, pointing at the pending entry that is FARTHEST from the gripper's [y, x] at this decision step (largest straight-line distance in image pixels); list position never chooses the cube. Point at that stored [y, x], or at the cube visible within a few pixels of it (cube positions wobble). If no cube is currently listed at that position it is merely hidden by the arm: still choose B at the stored point; never switch to another entry for that reason and never treat the list as empty."},
 {"modify_from": "apply rule 3 and choose B at the first carried entry.", "modify_to": "apply rule 3 and choose B at the carried entry farthest from the gripper."},
 {"modify_from": "else if any cube position is remembered in pending_cubes choose B at its first entry; else choose A.", "modify_to": "else if any cube position is remembered in pending_cubes choose B at the entry farthest from the gripper's current [y, x]; else choose A."}
],
"refused": "The round-1 ordering by x descending is replaced rather than kept: it was adopted as a heuristic fitting two of three episodes in that round, and this round it contradicted the recorded pick at every multi-cube decision, so it no longer settles anything and keeping it alongside a second criterion would only add a clause. The report's own rejected proposals stay out: smallest x / robot's rightmost first, largest y first, and 'the last entry of the list' each fit a single step and fail elsewhere; ordering by listing order of the highlighted areas, by distance from the button, or by colour was checked and fits nothing. The one episode whose picks were nearest-the-gripper is left unexplained; the report concludes the true order is a hidden spawn order nothing shown reveals, so no clause is added for it. Removal of an entry at pick-up by nearest-to-closing-position, retention of hidden cubes, and the placing-step no-change from round 1 are kept unchanged."}
